                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The markedly elevated PSA level is unexpected in a 71-year-old female, as PSA is typically not present at significant levels in women. This result may indicate a pre-analytical or analytical error, sample misidentification, or rare ectopic PSA production. Recommend immediate verification of patient/sample identity and repeat testing; clinical correlation is essential.</td>
